            <ArticleTitle>Obturator neuropathy after forceps delivery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47S-48S</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 31-year-old woman developed a disabling obturator neuropathy as a result of a difficult delivery. This was successfully diagnosed and treated by obturator nerve blocks with anesthetic and steroid at the obturator foramen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
